module System/Memory

### Several readers or one writer: `viewing g` lets other readers in at the same time, `modifying g` waits until it is
### the only one. Once a writer waits, readers that come later wait behind it, so a stream of readers can't keep a
### writer out. The state is one byte, and the runtime's AccessManager keeps who holds it: an agent that has to wait
### goes through the AccessManager, which stops the program when agents wait on each other (`[debug] deadlock-check`).
### :see: {AccessPolicy}, {Exclusive}, {Guarded}
record MultiRead
obeys AccessPolicy
    ### The byte whose access the AccessManager hands out: its address names this access.
    secret guard: U8

### Creates a free reader-writer access.
### :returns: The resulting `MultiRead` value.
routine MultiRead() -> MultiRead
    return MultiRead(guard: 0)

### The AccessManager's kind for this policy: a multi-read access.
### :returns: 2.
@readonly
routine MultiRead.access_kind() -> U32
    return 2
